  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Perched on the heights of Grimaud (592 chemin des Mûres), La Baie des Voiles is the restaurant of the Château Rose hotel, with a view over the Gulf of Saint-Tropez. The official website presents a Land &amp; Sea menu by the starred chef Christophe Chiavola; the Saint-Germain rooftop bar, from 6pm to midnight by reservation, is open in the same hotel.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The Grimaud tourist office names La Baie des Voiles on its "Dog-friendly restaurants" page ("if your dog is well-behaved and kept on a leash, it will be accepted in most restaurants; mention that you have a dog when booking") and its listing for the restaurant says "Pets accepted". The restaurant publishes no precise rule (dining room or terrace, dog size).</p>
      <p>As for hours, the tourist office announces opening from 4 April to 1 November 2026, every day from 8am to 2:30pm and from 7:30pm to 10:30pm: the 2026 season is over, 2027 dates are to be confirmed on 04 94 82 65 70.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: mention that you are coming with your dog when you book, as the tourist office recommends.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Grimaud tourist office also publishes pages on walks, beaches and outings with your dog in the town.</p>
